From: surface-kit
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: agc: damp steps while highlights clip

Pointed at a bright object the image flashed bright and dark: with part of
the image clipped the MSV no longer scales with the exposure, so a full
proportional step overshoots, the clipped area drops below the clip level,
and the next full step overshoots back. While the share of highlight
pixels is above highlightsLow, take half the step in log terms (the
square root of the factor); without highlights the full step stays, so
convergence elsewhere is unchanged.

ov8865: highlightsMinTarget 1.9 was above the target lowered to 1.6 in an
earlier patch, which turned highlight protection off; 1.2 restores it.

---
--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.cpp
@@ -174,6 +174,15 @@
 
 	double factor = std::clamp((target - 0.5) / std::max(exposureMSV - 0.5, 0.01),
 				   1.0 / kMaxStep, kMaxStep);
+	/*
+	 * With part of the image clipped the MSV no longer scales with the
+	 * exposure: a full step overshoots, the clipped area comes back below
+	 * the clip level, the next full step overshoots the other way, and a
+	 * bright object makes the image flash bright and dark. Take half the
+	 * step (in log terms) while there are highlights.
+	 */
+	if (highlights > highlightsLow_)
+		factor = std::sqrt(factor);
 	if (std::abs(exposureMSV - target) <= kDeadband)
 		factor = 1.0;
 	if (std::abs(factor - 1.0) < 0.03)
--- a/src/ipa/simple/data/ov8865.yaml
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/data/ov8865.yaml
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@
       highlightsLevel: 224
       highlightsLow: 0.005
       highlightsHigh: 0.03
-      highlightsMinTarget: 1.9
+      highlightsMinTarget: 1.2
   # contrast autofocus on the dw9719 VCM
   - Af:
       settleFrames: 2
